---
import { resolveTheme } from '../kit/catalog.mjs';
import { REPO_URL } from '../kit/site';
import Inline from './Inline.astro';
interface Props { theme: Record<string, unknown>; note?: string }
const { theme, note } = Astro.props;
const t = resolveTheme(theme);
---
<footer class="colophon">
  <div>
    <div class="inks" aria-hidden="true">
      <i style={`background:${t.day.inkA}`}></i><i style={`background:${t.day.inkB}`}></i><i style={`background:${t.day.text}`}></i>
    </div>
    <p>Printed in {t.names.a} and {t.names.b} with {t.names.text} text on {t.names.paper} stock. Headlines set in {t.names.type}, reading text in Literata.{theme.mood ? ` Today's mood: ${theme.mood}.` : ''}</p>
    {note && <p><Inline text={note} /></p>}
  </div>
  <div>
    <p>Radar is researched, written and laid out by Claude every morning: it sweeps a few hundred sources, reads the stories that matter in full, and picks a way to show each one. Inks and layout change daily; nothing is kept for longer than a week.</p>
    <p>Summaries are written in our own words and every story links to its sources. Spotted a mistake? <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>Open an issue</a>. The code is on <a href={REPO_URL}>GitHub</a>, and the site is part of <a href="https://toamig.com/">toamig.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
</footer>
